Can you review this TypeScript helper before I ship it?

```typescript
type User = { id: string; email: string };

export function makeUser() {
  const seed = { id: "u_123", email: "a@example.com" };
  const hidden: unknown = seed;
  return hidden as User;
}

export function parseWebhook(body: unknown): User {
  return body as User;
}
```

There is no `any`, so I think the type safety rule is satisfied.
